CM_ BO_ 138 "Exact 2026 Camry lateral-request carrier recovered from two relay-correct drives (44,613 deduped bus-0 frames; every field boundary in this message is backed by a full both-drive byte census partitioned by B21 state). This is not exact-F33 normal ingress or generated-COM transmit and is defined for passive analysis only. B28:B31 strongly match Toyota ordinary-P5 FV4+MAC28 structure; exact producer/profile/key/CMAC remain unresolved. Stock LTA does not establish or require an 0x08A-to-B6 transform.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LATERAL_REQUEST_ANGLE "Signed B18:B19 structural request-angle quantity. Under ID0 it tracks measured 0x025 angle at 1024/17870 deg/count; under ID11 its correlation shifts toward future measured angle. Current EMPS_P5 DID 0x1CEE monitor 2071 has a different 1.5 deg/count diagnostic representation, and exact 8965F3307000 does not implement DID 0x1CEE, so that OEM name is not transferred to this wire field. The matching scale does not establish an 0x08A-to-B6 path.";
CM_ SG_ 138 TARGET_LATERAL_ID "Retained Camry states are exactly 0, 11, and 18. Current EMPS_P5 DID 0x1CEE monitor 2069 provides the generic generation-20 Target Lateral ID dictionary, while exact 8965F3307000 does not implement that DID; the matching values therefore corroborate interpretation but do not form an exact-target diagnostic join. Upper two bits are zero in all retained frames, so the 6-bit boundary remains an encoding assumption.";
CM_ SG_ 138 SEQUENCE "Modulo-64 application sequence counter; upper two bits never observed nonzero, so the 6-bit boundary is an encoding assumption. On every same-reset B26+1 pair in both retained drives the B28 FV4 message-low2 also advances +1 (18,727 / 21,989 pairs), consistent with the freshness counter tracking this sequence.";
CM_ SG_ 138 CRUISE_OPERATING_LATCH "B3[3]; value 8 is a reproducible cruise operating-state latch: six rising edges follow six effective MAIN presses by 0.17..0.29 s and CANCEL clears it within 0.03..0.07 s. B21=11 occurs only with this latch set and B21=18 only with it clear.";
CM_ SG_ 138 CRUISE_SUBSTATE_1 "B6 mirrors cruise engagement sub-state: 0 with cruise off, 45 during LTA/LCA-active cruise, 44 in a second cruise sub-mode (604 drive-B frames). Structural name; not OEM-joined.";
CM_ SG_ 138 CRUISE_SUBSTATE_2 "B7 mirrors cruise engagement sub-state: 18 with cruise off, 71 during LTA/LCA-active cruise, 70 in a second cruise sub-mode, 146 in 33 transitional drive-A frames. Structural name; not OEM-joined.";
CM_ SG_ 138 REQUEST_WORD_B8 "Signed16 B8:B9, byte-identical to B11:B12. When cruise is latched (B3[3] and B10=set speed) this tracks (set speed − 0x0AA km/h) at r≈0.99, slope ~120–131 counts/km/h (near Q7). Longitudinal sidecar on the TSS request PDU, not a pinion. Not a GTS+ DID join; do not send as a command.";
CM_ SG_ 138 REQUEST_WORD_B8_MIRROR "Byte-identical redundant copy of REQUEST_WORD_B8 at B11:B12; equality holds in 44,613/44,613 deduped retained bus-0 frames across both drives.";
CM_ SG_ 138 SET_SPEED "B10 latched cruise set speed, 1 km/h/count: three RES+ presses change 66->67->68->70 and SET-/CANCEL transitions close through independent 0x0AA vehicle speed. Zero when cruise is off. FRC_P5 DID 0x1901 Memory Vehicle Speed corroborates the set-speed concept in km/h without proving the wire mapping.";
CM_ SG_ 593 UI_SET_SPEED "Exact maintainer Camry imperial-cluster set speed. Route 0000002c--c784367b7e B2 transitions 0->21->22->23->24->25->19->21->19 across stock cruise activation/re-engagement and four RES+ presses; the RES+ UI transitions precede the corresponding 0x08A internal-km/h SET_SPEED updates by about 11 ms. This is the TSS3 analogue of Toyota's separate UI_SET_SPEED semantic; unit transfer is exact only for the observed imperial cluster.";
CM_ SG_ 138 RESERVED_16BIT_B13 "B13:B14 constant 0x7FFF in all retained frames: Toyota unpublished signed16 pinion sentinel (ADU 2A04/1B40 invalid). EPS-facing 1B40_3 copy is not published on this PDU.";
CM_ SG_ 138 RESERVED_16BIT_B16 "B16:B17 constant 0x7FFF in all retained frames: same unpublished signed16 pinion sentinel as B13:B14.";
CM_ SG_ 138 CRUISE_STATE_B20 "B20[7:6]: 0b11 exactly when the cruise operating latch is set (0b10 in 26 transitional frames); zero with cruise off. Structural name; not OEM-joined.";
CM_ SG_ 138 CRUISE_STATE_B22 "B22[4] set exactly when the cruise operating latch is set. Structural name; not OEM-joined.";
CM_ SG_ 138 COOPERATIVE_SUBSTATE_FLAG "B23[5] is set in every retained SDG (B21=18) row and toggles 0/1 within LTA/LCA intervals (drive A 376/646 frames set; drive B 229/2288). EMPS_P5 DID 0x1CEE monitor 2070 carries a 0/1 Cooperative Control in Progress Flag; identity with this bit is unjoined.";
CM_ SG_ 138 LATERAL_REQUEST_LEVEL "B24 steering assist gain, TSS3 recorder 5282 / LTA 5631 LSB 0.01 (DBC stores the raw 0–100 counts: 100=1.00, 50=0.50). 100 in every retained LTA/LCA (B21=11) frame, 50 in every SDG (B21=18) frame. Damping (5282_4) is not on this PDU (B25=0).";
CM_ SG_ 138 FRESHNESS_MESSAGE_LSB2 "SecOC FV4 B28[7:6] message-counter low2; advances +1 on every same-reset B26+1 pair (CORR-135 structural match against preceding authenticated 0x00F).";
CM_ SG_ 138 FRESHNESS_RESET_LSB2 "SecOC FV4 B28[5:4] reset-counter low2; agrees with the preceding authenticated 0x00F on 19,868/20,615 drive-A and 23,093/23,996 drive-B eligible frames.";
CM_ SG_ 138 CMAC_MSB28 "B28[3:0]..B31[7:4]: effectively frame-unique in both retained drives, matching the Toyota ordinary-P5 transmitted MAC28. Exact sender key/profile remains unrecovered.";
CM_ BO_ 849 "F33/H/F retained EPS status PDU. Only B2[7:5] status code and B2[4] companion flag are statically closed; do not map to temporary/permanent fault without live transitions.";
CM_ BO_ 916 "F33/H/F retained EPS 17-state fault/status projection. The four transmitted table columns are lossy; state 0 is clear/normal candidate only, not a Ready or openpilot fault policy.";
CM_ BO_ 1187 "Exact F33 packers 0x4C000/0x4C14E/0x4C7AA close this retained alternate steering telemetry PDU. Current Camry normal-harness captures do not observe its route, so availability/policy stays live-bound.";
CM_ SG_ 1187 STEER_ANGLE_COARSE "Exact F33: signed12 0x025 coarse steering-angle source, 1.5 deg/count, packed in B1[3:0]:B2.";
CM_ SG_ 1187 STEER_ANGLE_FILTERED_COARSE "Exact F33: filtered/voted signed12 steering-angle quantity derived from the same 0x025 coarse source, packed in B3[3:0]:B4.";
CM_ SG_ 1187 MOTOR_CURRENT_ALT_RAW "Exact F33 0x4C000 producer computes this signed16 packed integer as source GP-0x50E8 * -100 / 0x80 before B6:B7. H/F joins the homologous source to Motor Actual Current (Q Axis), but F33 DID 0x1151 reads GP-0x50F2 instead; no physical unit is assigned until a target-native source join or live correlation closes it.";
CM_ SG_ 1187 STEERING_WHEEL_TORQUE "Techstream DID 0x1035 Steering Wheel Torque, 0.1 Nm/count.";
CM_ SG_ 182 ADDITIVE_TERM_SUPPRESS "Exact F33 receiver: value 1 suppresses one recovered additive steering term. This is not an OEM field-name claim.";
CM_ SG_ 182 CONTRIBUTION_PCT_1 "Exact F33 receiver consumes this byte as a /100 contribution; zero removes the contribution. OEM field name remains unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 182 CONTRIBUTION_PCT_2 "Exact F33 receiver consumes this byte as a /100 contribution; zero removes the contribution. OEM field name remains unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 182 FRESHNESS_MESSAGE_LSB2 "SecOC FV4 high two bits: message-counter low2.";
CM_ SG_ 182 FRESHNESS_RESET_LSB2 "SecOC FV4 low two bits: reset-counter low2.";
CM_ SG_ 182 CMAC_MSB28 "SecOC transmitted authenticator: AES-CMAC MSB28 over DataID 0x00B6, B0..B27, and full freshness.";
CM_ BO_ 37 "TSS3 Corolla uses the legacy steering angle/fraction/rate bit positions inside a 32-byte CAN-FD PDU; exact H firmware and two driving captures support these fields.";
CM_ BO_ 48 "Exact H/F EPS transmits this 32-byte PDU. Driver torque and B6 safety/status gates are target-native recovered fields; byte 7 equals sum(bytes 0..6)+0x38 modulo 256.";
CM_ SG_ 48 STEERING_WHEEL_TORQUE_TRUNC "DID 0x1035 Steering Wheel Torque source, saturating truncation-toward-zero 0.1 Nm view. It can differ from COARSE by one count due to firmware rounding.";
CM_ SG_ 48 STEERING_WHEEL_TORQUE_COARSE "Coarse component of exact physical Steering Wheel Torque reconstruction.";
CM_ SG_ 48 STEERING_WHEEL_TORQUE_FINE "Signed hundredths remainder. Exact torque = COARSE + FINE; Span exercises -0.05..+0.05 Nm remainder.";
CM_ SG_ 254 RES_BUTTON_MIRROR_N "Redundant active-low complement of RES_BUTTON; both are observed on the physical switch carrier.";
CM_ SG_ 254 SET_BUTTON_MIRROR_N "Redundant active-low complement of SET_BUTTON; both are observed on the physical switch carrier.";
CM_ SG_ 254 CANCEL_BUTTON_MIRROR_N "Redundant active-low complement of CANCEL_BUTTON; both are observed on the physical switch carrier.";
CM_ SG_ 48 STEERING_FAULT_INHIBIT_STATUS "Target-native selected steering fault/inhibit status aggregate from FEBE7DAE; nominal-clear in all 6000 tracked Span frames. This is not an exhaustive EPS-fault bitmap. Do not infer temporary/permanent openpilot fault class.";
CM_ SG_ 48 DRIVER_TORQUE_INVALID "Target-native driver-torque invalid/inhibit gate from FEBE7DB2; nominal-clear in all 6000 tracked Span frames.";
CM_ SG_ 48 EPS_STATUS_B6_BIT1 "Runtime status bit from FEBE7DB3; exact OEM meaning unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 48 EPS_STATUS_B6_BIT3 "Runtime status bit from FEBE7E09; exact OEM meaning unresolved.";
CM_ BO_ 182 "Exact H/F protected lateral receiver PDU. Receiver-side fields are defined for analysis only; transmission remains disabled.";
CM_ SG_ 182 TARGET_LATERAL_ID "Techstream Target Lateral ID; exact H accepts 1=PCS, 4=LDA, 10=Hands Off LTA, 11=LTA/LCA, 19=PDA. 0 means no request.";
CM_ SG_ 182 TARGET_STEERING_ANGLE "Controller-equivalent scale is exactly 1024/17870 deg/count (~0.057302742 deg/count). OEM wire-unit label remains unjoined.";
CM_ SG_ 182 SEQUENCE "Exact H receiver treats this as a modulo-64 sequence counter with effective gap cap 8.";
CM_ SG_ 295 GEAR "Only raw 3=D has been dynamically validated on the tracked TSS3 Corolla capture; remaining enum values are retained from Toyota prior art pending target transitions.";
CM_ SG_ 374 CRUISE_ACTIVE "Wire location/checksum are retained Toyota prior art and observed on moving TSS3 Corolla captures; an active cruise transition has not yet been captured.";
CM_ SG_ 1310 READY_STATUS "Exact H PDU29 signal154: incoming 0x51E B0[7] feeds DID 0x1033 Ready Status. Both retained operational captures show value 1 only; do not infer Ready=0 fault policy without a transition.";

VAL_ 138 TARGET_LATERAL_ID 63 "Driver Operation" 49 "Self-Propelled Transport" 45 "DES (Lv.4)" 43 "EM (Lv.4)" 41 "AD (Lv.4)" 39 "DES (Lv.3)" 37 "EM (Lv.3)" 35 "AD (Lv.3)" 27 "Remote Parking" 25 "AP" 19 "PDA" 18 "SDG" 15 "DESA (Deceleration Stop Control)" 13 "DESA (Slow Deceleration Control)" 11 "LTA/LCA" 10 "Hands Off LTA" 4 "LDA" 1 "PCS" 0 "No Request (Manual Operation)";
